{"tool_name":"scbio","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"scBio","home":"https://github.com/amitfrish/scBio/blob/master/README.md","license":"GPL-2.0","summary":"R pacakge containing a repository of methods aiming to understand complex processes related to the cellular variability within tissues.","addition_date":"2019-06-21T07:13:23Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T21:09:00.563366Z","tool_type":["Library"],"version":["0.1.5"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:scBio","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"amfrishberg@gmail.com","name":"Amit Frishberg","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Developer","Maintainer","Primary contact"]},{"name":"Irit Gat-Viks","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Developer"]},{"name":"Naama Peshes-Yaloz","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Developer"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://github.com/amitfrish/scBio/blob/master/README.md"},{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/scBio/scBio.pdf"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Deisotoping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3629"},{"term":"Enrichment analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3501"},{"term":"Genotyping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3196"}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"scBio","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Ruta","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/s41592-019-0355-5","metadata":{"abstract":"Single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) is a rich resource of cellular heterogeneity, opening new avenues in the study of complex tissues. We introduce Cell Population Mapping (CPM), a deconvolution algorithm in which reference scRNA-seq profiles are leveraged to infer the composition of cell types and states from bulk transcriptome data (\u2018scBio\u2019 CRAN R-package). Analysis of individual variations in lungs of influenza-virus-infected mice reveals that the relationship between cell abundance and clinical symptoms is a cell-state-specific property that varies gradually along the continuum of cell-activation states. The gradual change is confirmed in subsequent experiments and is further explained by a mathematical model in which clinical outcomes relate to cell-state dynamics along the activation process. Our results demonstrate the power of CPM in reconstructing the continuous spectrum of cell states within heterogeneous tissues.","authors":[{"name":"Amit I."},{"name":"Bacharach E."},{"name":"Cohn O."},{"name":"Frishberg A."},{"name":"Gat-Viks I."},{"name":"Iraqi F.A."},{"name":"Mandelboim M."},{"name":"Mayo L."},{"name":"Peshes-Yaloz N."},{"name":"Rosentul D."},{"name":"Steuerman Y."},{"name":"Valadarsky L."},{"name":"Yankovitz G."}],"citationCount":76,"date":"2019-04-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nature Methods","title":"Cell composition analysis of bulk genomics using single-cell data"},"pmcid":"PMC6443043","pmid":"30886410","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Cell biology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2229"},{"term":"Infectious disease","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3324"},{"term":"Transcriptomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3308"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"scBio","home":"https://bio.tools/scBio","license":"GPL-2.0","version":"0.1.5","summary":"R pacakge containing a repository of methods aiming to understand complex processes related to the cellular variability within tissues.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:scbio:0.1.5/lib/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":false,"sourcecode":{"free":null,"interpreted":true,"license":null,"public":true,"readme":false,"repository":{"anonymous":null,"online":null}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"d